The kit was extracted from Wappie (github.com/thehappieco/wappie, Apache-2.0)
at commit 8c0c1f74103bc6bb65a93b13613ad1964d4399c4: the Go package
internal/crypto/seal, the request signature of internal/mcpauth/hmac.go, and
the browser cryptography of packages/client/src/crypto. The vectors under
vectors/wappie were produced by Wappie's own code at that commit.

The platform profile (profiles/platform, js/src/profiles/platform.ts and
js/src/internal) was taken from The Happie Co platform
(github.com/thehappieco/platform, Apache-2.0) at commit
5e66d841145b33dcd73cd575f2816a866793d774: the Go package
internal/crypto/idcrypto and the browser cryptography of web/shared/crypto.
The vectors under vectors/platform were produced by the platform's own code
at that commit.

Part 2 of the platform profile and the relying party (profiles/platform,
oidcrp, js/src/oidc-rp.ts and js/src/internal) were taken from the platform
at commit 4476bf4b446297ee2b74a6f032fede7786345327: internal/crypto/idcrypto
(key delivery, PKCE), web/shared/crypto (keydelivery.ts, pkce.ts, x25519.ts,
hpkebase.ts), web/shared/oidc-rp, and tools/fakeproduct (the userinfo call and
the pin). The vectors key-delivery.json, pkce.json and
password-stream-safe.json were produced by the platform's code at that
commit.

Part 3 of the platform profile (profiles/platform/passkey.go and
extensions.go; js/src/internal/platform/passkey.ts and extensions.ts) was
taken from the platform at commit b5d9f69a4836736e792914b20d7c2c4ce573fedf:
internal/crypto/idcrypto (passkey.go, extensions.go, json.go) and
web/shared/crypto (passkey.ts, and the allowlist of webauthn.ts). The
vectors passkey.json and client-extensions.json were produced by the
platform's code at that commit.

The relying party rule of the platform profile (passkey.EndsInANumber and
profiles/platform.ValidRPID; js/src/passkey.ts endsInANumber and isRPID)
follows the platform at commit 75b6b940df5c6903023f9030f5f3875540f6a36f.
The vector file rp-id-ends-in-number.json and the generator under
vectors/platform/_generators-75b6b94 were produced by and copied from the
platform's code at that commit, which the platform's handoff of 2026-10-05
places under the kit's license. Version 2 of the KDF worker's protocol
(js/src/internal/kdf.ts and kdfrun.ts) follows the platform's
web/shared/crypto/kdf.ts, argon2.ts and kdf.worker.ts at that commit.

Wappie's platform wrap (profiles/wappie/platformwrap.go and
js/src/internal/wappie/platformwrap.ts) was taken from Wappie's console
(github.com/thehappieco/wappie-cloud) at commit
3bfee279581ad15f6d2d2db3d3a9794c8eac50ca: platformwrap/ and
web/platform/platformWrap.ts, with the first byte of a wrap changed from
0x01 to 0x03. The vectors platform-wrap-go.json and platform-wrap-ts.json
under vectors/wappie/golden, and platform-wrap-vectors.json under
vectors/wappie/legacy, were produced by the console's code at that commit
with that change (vectors/wappie/_generators/cloud/header-0x03.patch).

THCSEAL v1 and its key wrappers (thcseal, kms, kms/awskms and kms/localkek)
were taken from the platform at commit
d32b6632a45f1fc5a1884bb4fbe02d8ec8c74371: internal/seal and internal/kms,
with the tests of commit d3e8c6d6cdf886b02f135a7067a3de02a576528e, which
replace the platform's AWS identifiers with AWS's documentation
placeholders. The platform's handoff of 2026-10-08 places them under the
kit's license. The vector file thcseal-v1.json under
vectors/platform/thcseal-v1 was produced by the platform's code at that
commit.

